WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.853 --> 00:00:10.817
This page is your course map. Our class meets live most weeks, and everything around the class lives here: every week is a station on one journey.

2
00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:21.866
Read the class rhythm panel first. The panel near the top tells you what to do before and after this week's class, or how an independent week runs. It updates as the term moves.

3
00:00:21.866 --> 00:00:32.010
Find the current week. The This Week card and the highlighted station show where the course is right now. Click any station to open that week's page.

4
00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:43.028
Read the delivery label before you click. The legend marks live class weeks, asynchronous weeks with no lecture, and Study Week. Weeks 4 and 11 are independent learning weeks; Weeks 13 and 14 turn the class window into office hours.

5
00:00:43.028 --> 00:00:54.038
Use the Study Compass. The compass box suggests what to do next based on what you have already done on this device. A few fixed rules run in your browser; no AI and no server. It is a suggestion, never a requirement.

6
00:00:54.038 --> 00:01:05.046
Pick your program lens if you want one. The Viewing as chip personalizes examples to your field of study. The course content stays the same for everyone; only the framing changes. Choose or change it any time on Career Choices.

7
00:01:05.046 --> 00:01:09.746
Nothing on this page is graded or reported to your professor.

8
00:01:09.746 --> 00:01:15.191
Where next: Open the current week's station and check how that week runs.
